Lerroux’s government falls immediately [? if prrs_leader == "Gordón Ordás" : , not even PRRS' votes can save the situation ?]. After the failure of Lerroux, president Alcalá-Zamora tasks Diego Martínez Barrio, second in charge inside the PRR to form a new republican government.

Socialist president of the Cortes, Julián Besteiro has asked the PSOE executive to support Barrio's government to ensure the parliamentary wellbeing. [? if prrs_leader == "Gordón Ordás" : However, PRRS' leadership makes that impossible ?]. If this government fails again the President of the Republic will dissolve the Cortes and call for new legislative elections in a context of growing conservative forces.

